Application Health Monitoring with Argo CD
Objectives
Design and deploy a Lua-based custom health check system in Argo CD that evaluates Deployment, Service, and ConfigMap resources beyond default status conditions
Implement a webhook-driven notification pipeline that fires on health state transitions and delivers structured payloads to a receiver service running inside the cluster
Validate end-to-end observability by injecting deliberate failures, confirming degraded state detection, and verifying recovery propagation through the notification chain
Prerequisites
Comfort with Linux command-line operations including file editing, process management, and reading structured log output
Conceptual understanding of Kubernetes primitives (Pods, Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps) and how controllers reconcile desired versus actual state
Familiarity with Git repository operations sufficient to commit changes and observe downstream sync behavior
Lab Environment
You will work on a dedicated AWS EC2 Ubuntu instance provided by Al Nafi. The instance has a base Ubuntu installation; you will install all required tools in Task 1.

