Troubleshooting
If your Lua health script is syntactically valid but Argo CD continues showing the default health status rather than your custom evaluation, what mechanism would you use to confirm that the argocd-cm patch was actually read by the application controller after its restart, and how would you distinguish a configuration-load failure from a logic error in the script itself?

If the webhook receiver pod is running and its Service exists, but the Argo CD Notifications controller logs show repeated connection refused errors to your receiver URL, what sequence of in-cluster network diagnostics would you perform to isolate whether the problem is DNS resolution, Service selector mismatch, or the receiver process not binding to the expected address and port?

Conclusion
This lab demonstrated how Argo CD's Lua-based health evaluation layer can be extended beyond built-in defaults to encode application-specific correctness criteria, and how the Notifications controller transforms those health state transitions into actionable signals delivered to external systems. The failure injection scenarios established that the pipeline detects real degradation conditions â not just configuration correctness â and that recovery is propagated through the same channel without manual intervention. These patterns form the operational foundation for GitOps workflows where automated health feedback replaces manual cluster inspection.
